WEBVTT

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.310
My parents went on a trip,

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.560
and won't be back until tomorrow afternoon.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:15.600
So you'll have the house all to yourself today.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.590
You're going to make dinner by yourself?

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:18.690
Wow.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.190
Yeah, so... anyway...

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:23.400
It's got really cold lately.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.110
I wish I'd worn a scarf.

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:27.200
Can we stop by the bookstore?

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:27.950
Sure.

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:33.120
If you're lonely, just say so!

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:37.350
What's this?

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:38.880
Are you going somewhere?

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.500
We're having a sleepover at Aya-chan's house.

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:44.380
Alice, are you ready?

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.230
Let's go.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:47.010
Okay.

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:52.680
You don't need any of these things.

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:56.130
You don't really need a dictionary, do you?

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:58.190
But it's my Bible!

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:03.780
Let's stop by Karen's house and go to Aya-chan's place together.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.990
She lives somewhere around here...

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:09.190
It must be this apartment building.

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:12.660
Hmm, which room is hers?

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:13.950
All of them.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:16.750
What?

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:18.580
The whole building is Karen's house.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.170
Thanks for waiting.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.280
Welcome!

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:34.100
I've been waiting for you.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.560
Thanks for having us.

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:40.440
Where's Youko-chan?

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:42.190
She's not here yet.

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:43.480
You must've been cold walking here.

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:45.320
Come on inside.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:51.070
Your hands are cold.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:54.280
Were you waiting outside the whole time?

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:58.200
You were late getting here, so I got worried...

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.040
I mean, I wasn't worried at all!

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:32.260
Thanks for waiting.

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:33.800
Sorry, sorry.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:35.890
The convenience store was packed.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:37.470
Snacks!

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:38.390
Hooray.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:41.140
We only just got here, too.

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:43.770
Your room is so cute, Aya.

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:45.510
R-Really?

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:47.770
Karen, don't open that!

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:50.110
Your secret stash?

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:52.360
No, it's, um...

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:54.110
That's her underwear drawer.

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:56.730
How did you know?!

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:57.500
What?

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:59.120
Just a hunch...

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:00.540
X-ray vision?!

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:03.260
No...

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:06.910
I'll make dinner.

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:08.540
We'll help you.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:09.790
I'll help, too.

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:11.550
You got it!

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:12.800
What are you making?

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:16.090
Well, meat with potatoes, and...

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:19.600
I feel like I'm forgetting something...

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:28.610
Now, then...

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:32.900
What do we season it with?

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:35.150
Start by adding two tablespoons of soy sauce.

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:36.110
Got it.

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:40.590
Measure it out properly!

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:43.040
Doing it by eye works fine for this stuff.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:45.410
I'll do it!

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:49.080
Honestly, it's great that you're so generous,

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:50.790
but you're just too imprecise!

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:54.050
Is that a compliment or an insult?!

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:56.550
Can you break the eggs into here for me?

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:58.380
Okay!

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:04.200
By the way, I saw someone breaking eggs on their head the other day.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.680
I've seen someone do that, too!

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:09.940
Hey, Alice, Karen... Have you broken those eggs?

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:16.740
You're supposed to break boiled eggs on your head, not raw eggs.

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:20.780
The bath is all warmed up, so go clean yourselves.

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:22.780
I want a bubble bath.

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:23.790
Bubbles?

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.080
I'm sorry, but I don't have any of that.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:28.250
Oh, I do have scented bath powder, though.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:32.420
Which would you like?

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:33.340
One that smells like flowers?

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:36.050
I want a wooden tub.

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:37.090
A real one.

00:05:37.090 --> 00:05:40.890
That's also... not possible.

00:05:57.110 --> 00:06:01.610
Blonde girls bathing is a work of art.

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:02.990
How?!

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:08.160
There's some kind of hair spray.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:09.540
Do you think it's Ayaya's?

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:11.580
I'll just borrow a little.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:13.370
It's so smooth.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:14.420
So cold.

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:16.750
Oh, this is for hair regrowth...

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:17.460
You're so mean!

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:18.450
I bet you did that on purpose!

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:19.480
I didn't.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:21.380
It's written in kanji, so I couldn't read it!

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:23.220
Geez!

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:27.890
Thanks for the food.

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:38.150
Delicious!

00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:40.570
I'm glad.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.240
Thanks for the wonderful food.

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:44.320
You flatter me.

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:46.620
By the way, Shino,

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:51.290
you said you felt like you'd forgotten something important earlier.

00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:52.670
Have you remembered what it was?

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:54.330
Not yet...

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:56.350
Oh, that's it!

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:57.710
I just remembered!

00:06:58.210 --> 00:07:02.800
My mother made us meat with potatoes for dinner.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:04.740
Have some.

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:06.850
You have terrible timing!

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:11.770
Thanks for coming to stay tonight.

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:14.520
I had fun, thanks to all of you.

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:15.900
If I'd been by myself,

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:18.020
I'm sure I wouldn't have got to sleep tonight.

00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:21.490
So scary.

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:27.870
Why do you all like scary stories?!

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:28.410
Huh?

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:31.960
You want to join us in telling scary stories after all?

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:33.460
I do!

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:38.090
Mornin'.

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:39.340
Morning.

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:41.160
Good morning.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.300
Breakfast is ready.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:45.510
Oh, it looks delicious.

00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:46.300
Hooray!

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:47.470
Fried eggs!

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:49.930
Good morning.

00:07:51.350 --> 00:07:52.430
<i>Her hair...</i>

00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:57.480
What...

00:07:58.870 --> 00:07:59.900
What?!

00:07:59.900 --> 00:08:00.610
Huh?

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:02.150
What do you mean, "What?"

00:08:02.570 --> 00:08:04.650
You've got serious bed hair.

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:13.330
Sensei, are you any good at tongue twisters?

00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:15.790
Namamyugi namagomi nyama-

00:08:15.790 --> 00:08:19.210
They're difficult for people accustomed to speaking English.

00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:21.130
Is she a foreigner?

00:08:23.630 --> 00:08:27.720
Namyamugi na-

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:31.600
I wish someone would teach me the trick to saying tongue twisters!

00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:33.980
What?

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:35.730
Komichi-san!

00:08:42.530 --> 00:08:46.550
Japanese uniforms are so cute.

00:08:46.550 --> 00:08:50.280
You don't see many sailor-style uniforms in England?

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:51.700
I mean the stiff-collared ones.

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:52.640
They look like black cats.

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:54.040
It's so cute.

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:56.330
That's the boys' uniform.

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:57.240
What?

00:08:57.240 --> 00:08:59.210
I bet it'd look good on girls, too.

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:01.540
We should live more freely!

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:03.260
We must value our individuality!

00:09:04.550 --> 00:09:06.720
You tend to dress down a lot, though...

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:15.060
It was fun how it kinda felt like a field trip.

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:17.640
It reminded me of when you came to stay with us.

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:20.200
Come to my place next time.

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:20.950
Sure.

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:23.230
I'd like to visit your place.

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:25.300
You'll each get your own room.

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:32.720
Huh?

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:35.500
Ayaya, are you worried about something?

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:39.040
The weather is beautiful again today.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:43.710
You always have so much energy, Karen.

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:46.340
I wish I could be as open and free as you.

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:48.470
Oh, freedom!

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:50.480
I know.

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:51.840
I have a good idea.

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:56.130
Karen... I mean, Master!

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:57.890
Make me your apprentice!

00:09:57.890 --> 00:09:58.600
What?!

00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:02.110
I've looked up to you since the day we met!

00:10:02.610 --> 00:10:05.360
What should I do to become more like you?

00:10:07.780 --> 00:10:09.110
That sounds fun!

00:10:09.110 --> 00:10:12.240
I'll be your master today, okay?

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:13.990
Yes, please!

00:10:14.370 --> 00:10:15.370
In that case...

00:10:19.330 --> 00:10:22.670
W-What are you doing in public?!

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:29.050
I thought a good place to start would be by looking like me.

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:33.300
Wearing this won't make me like you.

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:36.220
You're right.

00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:38.850
Then start by copying the way I talk.

00:10:38.850 --> 00:10:39.930
Your broken Japanese?

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:41.810
O-Okay, then.

00:10:41.810 --> 00:10:43.770
No, more fluently.

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:46.440
L-Like this?!

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:49.070
How am I supposed to speak broken Japanese fluently?

00:10:49.070 --> 00:10:50.150
That doesn't make sense!

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:52.030
Don't worry about it!

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:55.160
Next, let's put it to practice during class!

00:10:57.910 --> 00:11:00.660
Komichi-san, could you answer this question?

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:01.940
Yes.

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:04.420
I...

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:06.750
I am sorry, but I don't understand!

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:14.390
Aya, are you okay?!

00:11:14.390 --> 00:11:16.950
Oh my god!

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:18.850
Calm down!

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:23.390
Master, I feel something's wrong here...

00:11:23.390 --> 00:11:24.250
No, no.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:25.900
You're doing well.

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:27.160
Aya.

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:29.230
Youko.

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:32.320
Are you playing tag?

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:34.200
I-I'm not running away or anything...

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:36.660
Huh?

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:40.390
Ayaya, here we go!

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:47.340
Karen, can't you be a little gentler?

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:49.620
Nope.

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:52.220
Today, I am your master.

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:54.550
You will call me Demon Coach Karen.

00:11:54.550 --> 00:11:56.220
Not "Master"?!

00:11:57.180 --> 00:12:01.260
Youko-chan, you're not pairing up with Aya-chan today?

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:06.020
No, she seems to be avoiding me today.

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:07.480
I'm sure it's just your imagination.

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:09.860
Why don't you join us, then?

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:11.860
We're playing volleyball, huh?

00:12:11.860 --> 00:12:13.230
No, kemari.

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:15.110
You're supposed to kick it with your feet.

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:19.450
Okay, I'll teach you the basics.

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:25.080
<i>Learning to be someone new is exhausting...</i>

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:28.630
Let's go hang out with the Archery Club next.

00:12:29.710 --> 00:12:32.920
In this game, you're supposed to hit the centre of the target.

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:35.260
They let me play the other day.

00:12:35.260 --> 00:12:36.060
What?!

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:37.470
No way!

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:41.350
Karen is good at competitive sports.

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:44.530
Even when she doesn't know the rules, she ends up doing well.

00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:48.490
<i>I can't copy that.</i>

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:51.560
<i>Karen must be some kind of genius.</i>

00:12:52.780 --> 00:12:57.110
I-I don't think I can be like you, Karen...

00:12:57.700 --> 00:13:00.700
Ayaya, why do you want to be like me?

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:02.370
Well...

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:06.290
I admire your old-fashioned style, Ayaya.

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:07.120
Huh?

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:10.710
I think you're best just as you are.

00:13:10.710 --> 00:13:11.880
Karen...

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:18.510
Ayaya?!

00:13:18.510 --> 00:13:20.090
What's wrong?

00:13:20.090 --> 00:13:21.410
Aya-chan?

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:28.140
You had a fight with Youko?

00:13:30.230 --> 00:13:34.030
Actually, I said some pretty awful things to her...

00:13:34.610 --> 00:13:36.650
I can never be honest with her.

00:13:36.650 --> 00:13:39.030
I'm always saying mean things to her.

00:13:39.030 --> 00:13:40.280
Oh, my.

00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:42.010
You're a tsundere, huh?

00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:45.410
If I were you, I'd make up with her.

00:13:45.750 --> 00:13:48.870
Ayaya, this is today's last mission.

00:13:49.210 --> 00:13:50.120
Huh?

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:51.380
What do you mean by "mission"?

00:13:51.380 --> 00:13:53.750
Go, Ayaya!

00:13:58.800 --> 00:14:00.150
Youko!

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:00.970
Aya.

00:14:00.970 --> 00:14:02.800
I-I need to talk to you!

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:03.640
About what?

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:06.220
I want to buy a notebook.

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:08.230
Will you come to the stationery store with me?

00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:09.290
Okay.

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:12.340
No...

00:14:12.340 --> 00:14:14.270
What?

00:14:17.900 --> 00:14:20.530
Maybe I'll buy a new notebook, too.

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:22.740
Listen, Youko...

00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:24.280
Sorry about this morning.

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:25.910
For what?

00:14:26.450 --> 00:14:27.540
I...

00:14:32.710 --> 00:14:34.380
I was so mean to you...

00:14:34.380 --> 00:14:36.050
You meant <i>that?!</i>

00:14:36.050 --> 00:14:37.170
Well, I...

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:40.700
I'm not mad about that at all.

00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:42.640
Really?

00:14:42.640 --> 00:14:44.250
What a relief.

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:47.010
I was convinced you hated me.

00:14:47.010 --> 00:14:47.520
What?

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:48.310
I don't hate you!

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:52.060
Let's make up by buying matching notebooks.

00:14:54.810 --> 00:14:56.570
How about this one?

00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:00.320
<i>It's so cute...</i>

00:15:01.070 --> 00:15:04.260
<i>She doesn't even like flowers.</i>

00:15:04.270 --> 00:15:05.770
<i>Oh, Youko.</i>

00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:09.500
<i>If Karen were here...</i>

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:11.940
Wow, Youko.

00:15:11.940 --> 00:15:12.940
It's so cute.

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:14.080
Thank you.

00:15:15.670 --> 00:15:16.750
Youko.

00:15:19.260 --> 00:15:22.340
T-Thanks!

00:15:35.270 --> 00:15:39.110
So you were trying to copy Karen, huh?

00:15:39.110 --> 00:15:41.360
Your broken Japanese was so cute.

00:15:41.360 --> 00:15:43.320
Ayaya still has a long way to go.

00:15:43.320 --> 00:15:46.820
Watch my great impersonation of Ayaya!

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:47.940
What?

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:51.620
I am Komichi Aya!

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:55.580
I can do anything when it comes to academics!

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:00.750
That's just Karen.

00:16:00.750 --> 00:16:02.920
It's Karen.

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:05.090
Oh, no!

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:42.720
So, yeah...

00:16:42.720 --> 00:16:45.220
I spilled some tea on it yesterday.

00:16:45.220 --> 00:16:46.720
Youko, you idiot!

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:48.690
Why are you calling me an idiot?!

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:52.320
Aya, you're acting like you did yesterday.

00:16:53.470 --> 00:16:55.850
You have failed as my apprentice.

00:18:27.610 --> 00:18:29.650
Let's play hide and seek!

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:31.610
Hide and what?

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:33.780
You mean, hide-and-go-seek?

00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:37.160
I wanted to make sure I played it when I came to Japan.

00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:38.700
Sounds good.

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:39.660
Let's play.

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:41.040
Okay!

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:43.750
You can hide anywhere in the school.

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:45.630
Let's play!

00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:50.130
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:18:50.430 --> 00:18:52.760
Okay, I'll count to thirty.

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:58.770
One, two, three...

00:18:59.480 --> 00:19:03.690
<i>She'll never guess that I've stayed in the starting room.</i>

00:19:03.690 --> 00:19:07.020
<i>Soon you'll witness the power of the hide and seek master, Karen...</i>

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:07.820
Huh?!

00:19:07.820 --> 00:19:10.030
I found Karen.

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:22.410
<i>There are so many places to hide in the school.</i>

00:19:23.750 --> 00:19:25.790
<i>This reminds me of elementary school...</i>

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:29.130
<i>...when I was the only one who wasn't found,</i>

00:19:29.130 --> 00:19:32.240
<i>and everyone went home without me.</i>

00:19:39.420 --> 00:19:41.350
Marco!

00:19:41.350 --> 00:19:43.270
Karen, that's the wrong game.

00:19:43.270 --> 00:19:45.190
Also, keep your voice down in the library.

00:19:45.520 --> 00:19:46.610
<i>Karen?!</i>

00:19:46.610 --> 00:19:48.440
<i>Did Youko find her already?</i>

00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:56.910
There doesn't seem to be anyone in here.

00:19:56.910 --> 00:19:59.370
Okay, let's look somewhere else.

00:19:59.730 --> 00:20:00.740
<i>What?!</i>

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:01.610
<i>Hey!</i>

00:20:01.610 --> 00:20:03.500
<i>Search harder!</i>

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:05.650
<i>They're leaving.</i>

00:20:05.650 --> 00:20:06.250
<i>Wait...</i>

00:20:06.750 --> 00:20:08.460
I'm right here!

00:20:08.460 --> 00:20:09.590
What?!

00:20:09.590 --> 00:20:11.340
She turned herself in?!

00:20:14.880 --> 00:20:17.220
S-Sorry for getting in your way.

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:18.430
What do you mean?

00:20:18.430 --> 00:20:20.350
Let's find Alice and Shino next.

00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:33.860
I should have hidden with Shino.

00:20:35.740 --> 00:20:37.160
I'm so sleepy...

00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:43.660
I don't know about Alice, but Shino's good at this game.

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:44.580
Really?

00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:47.200
We used to play hide-and-go-seek a lot.

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:49.700
Shino can erase her entire presence.

00:20:50.960 --> 00:20:53.300
She hides so silently,

00:20:53.300 --> 00:20:55.970
it made me wonder if she was a ninja in a past life.

00:20:56.680 --> 00:20:58.300
<i>How can she say that with a straight face?</i>

00:20:59.680 --> 00:21:02.570
Karen, that's a cute handkerchief.

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:05.390
Oh, this?

00:21:06.980 --> 00:21:09.520
I bought it in England. I like it a lot...

00:21:12.440 --> 00:21:16.360
Karen, can I touch your handkerchief?

00:21:16.360 --> 00:21:18.280
Where did you drop from?!

00:21:18.740 --> 00:21:21.900
With wings growing out of its face...

00:21:21.900 --> 00:21:22.910
Oh?

00:21:23.320 --> 00:21:25.910
The door to the art room is open...

00:21:27.020 --> 00:21:28.230
Alice-san?

00:21:28.230 --> 00:21:29.570
What happened?!

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:31.540
This is...

00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:35.590
A dying message?!

00:21:36.220 --> 00:21:37.330
<i>No, Sakura.</i>

00:21:37.330 --> 00:21:39.090
<i>You're just in shock.</i>

00:21:39.090 --> 00:21:41.970
<i>You must trust your students!</i>

00:21:43.090 --> 00:21:45.970
Alice-san!

00:21:47.980 --> 00:21:49.770
You were just asleep?

00:21:49.770 --> 00:21:50.710
I'm sorry.

00:21:50.710 --> 00:21:52.480
I jumped to conclusions.

00:21:53.020 --> 00:21:55.320
To make up for it, I'll hide with you!

00:21:55.320 --> 00:21:56.530
<i>What?!</i>

00:21:56.530 --> 00:22:00.070
<i>Now I can't say "I wish they'd hurry up and find me!"</i>

00:22:00.740 --> 00:22:02.450
She's not here.

00:22:02.450 --> 00:22:04.080
Alice.

00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:07.830
We haven't looked in here yet.

00:22:08.170 --> 00:22:11.040
Alice is so hard to find because she's small.

00:22:12.210 --> 00:22:14.460
Alice-san, keep quiet.

00:22:18.400 --> 00:22:23.680
Karasuma-sensei, what are you doing here?

00:22:23.680 --> 00:22:24.540
Huh?

00:22:24.540 --> 00:22:26.680
Um, I...

00:22:27.560 --> 00:22:30.940
<i>I'm supposed to be helping her hide, but they found me.</i>

00:22:30.940 --> 00:22:33.270
<i>I'm so clumsy.</i>

00:22:33.270 --> 00:22:35.570
R-Run...

00:22:35.570 --> 00:22:39.440
Alice-san, save yourself!

00:22:41.820 --> 00:22:45.410
I can't believe you fell asleep while hiding.

00:22:45.410 --> 00:22:47.450
You're so cute, Alice.

00:22:47.450 --> 00:22:49.160
B-But...

00:22:49.160 --> 00:22:51.040
That was fun!

00:22:51.040 --> 00:22:52.620
It's nice every once in a while.

00:22:53.130 --> 00:22:56.130
I'm glad you all enjoyed it.

00:22:56.550 --> 00:22:58.510
Okay, let's play tag next.

00:22:58.890 --> 00:23:01.130
Try to catch me.

00:23:01.510 --> 00:23:02.870
Bye, Karen.

00:23:02.870 --> 00:23:04.090
Laters.

00:23:04.090 --> 00:23:06.140
Go home before it gets dark.

00:23:06.140 --> 00:23:07.640
Oh...

00:23:08.140 --> 00:23:09.140
I get it!

00:23:09.140 --> 00:23:11.020
"Later", huh?

00:23:11.020 --> 00:23:13.060
That's not what I meant!

00:23:13.060 --> 00:23:16.920
Alice, what's tag called in English?

00:23:16.920 --> 00:23:19.990
It's called "Tag".

00:23:21.690 --> 00:23:24.320
I can't sleep after hearing those scary stories...

00:23:24.320 --> 00:23:26.920
Why don't you cuddle up to a stuffed toy while you sleep?

00:23:26.920 --> 00:23:28.390
I couldn't do that.

00:23:28.390 --> 00:23:31.260
Then, is there anything else you can cuddle instead?

00:23:31.870 --> 00:23:32.440
What?

00:23:32.440 --> 00:23:34.040
Me?

00:23:34.040 --> 00:23:35.910
See you next time.
